<title>MEXICO: Mexican 96-yr-old labor boss still unable to work.</title>
<headline>Mexican 96-yr-old labor boss still unable to work.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 96-year-old leader of Mexico's most important labor group is recovering well from an intestinal infection, but still has not returned to work, the Mexican Workers Confederation (CTM) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Fidel Velazquez, leader of the six-million-strong CTM and stalwart supporter of the ruling Institutional Revolutionary Party (PRI), was hospitalized for two weeks with the infection.</p>
<p>&quot;He is doing well...but doctors insist he rest at least another week,&quot; substitute CTM secretary general Leonardo Rodriguez told reporters. Velazquez will return to work as soon as doctors allow, he added.</p>
<p>((--Veronica Galan, Mexico newsroom +525 728-9553))</p>
